{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And HaShem went as soon as He finished, etc.</b> Meaning: immediately upon concluding His reply to Abraham — ״לֹא אַשְׁחִית בַּעֲבוּר הָעֲשָׂרָה״ — HaShem departed, and did not give him opportunity to pray for less than this number, either because Abraham had already said ״וַאֲדַבְּרָה אַךְ הַפַּעַם״ and would not speak further on this matter, or because HaShem knows that there would be no defense for fewer than ten. And although we find in the Rashbi (Zohar vol. I 105b) who said ״וְצַדִּיק יְסוֹד עוֹלָם״, it is possible that this applies when the righteous one is extraordinary, and it is possible that if Abraham had been within Sodom itself, he would have saved the entire city."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:16.392479797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}